  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "identifier": "dseams",
  "description": "Structural analysis of water and ice in molecular dynamics trajectories, using the 'd-SEAMS' engine (Goswami, Goswami and Singh (2020) <doi:10.1021/acs.jcim.0c00031>). Reads 'LAMMPS' dumps and 'XYZ' files on every build. When 'chemfiles' is found at build time, also reads the formats that library reads (PDB, GRO, DCD, and the rest of the chemfiles 0.10 set). When 'readcon-core' is found, also reads readcon '.con' files. readcon-core also defines '.convel'; this engine routes '.con'. Returns data frames for 'CHILL+' ice labels (Nguyen and Molinero (2015) <doi:10.1021/jp510289t>), primitive rings (Franzblau (1991) <doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.44.4925>), cages, Steinhardt q4 and q6 (Steinhardt, Nelson and Ronchetti (1983) <doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.28.784>), hydrogen bonds, radial distribution functions, prisms, domains, monolayers, topological fingerprints, coordination, density profiles, and jump_tau90. The engine is compiled from bundled C++ sources.",
